rows.old_statement_tex:
\label{thm:intro-high-dimensional}
Let \(\d\geq12\).  Every probability density of finite entropy satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \Hr(\rho\mid\muunif)
 \geq\frac12\sum_{k\in\Z^\d\setminus\{0\}}|k|^{-\d}|\wh\rho(k)|^2,
 \label{eq:intro-high-dual}
\end{equation}
with equality if and only if \(\rho\equiv1\).  Equivalently, every real \(u\in H^{\d/2}(\T^\d)\) satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \log\int_{\T^\d}e^{u-\bar u}\,\dd\muunif
 \leq\frac{1}{2(2\pi)^\d}\Ebo_\d(u),
 \label{eq:intro-high-primal}
\end{equation}
with equality if and only if \(u\) is constant.  In particular,
\begin{equation}
 \betagm(\d)=\betas(\d),
 \qquad
 \Azero(\d)=\As(\d).
 \label{eq:intro-high-threshold}
\end{equation}

There exists \(\varepsilon_\d>0\) such that, for
\begin{equation}
 \betas(\d)<\be<\betas(\d)+\varepsilon_\d,
 \label{eq:intro-onset-range}
\end{equation}
every global minimizer belongs, modulo translation, to the full \(\d\)-mode Morse--Bott branch.  More precisely, writing
\begin{equation}
 \delta:=1-\frac{\betas(\d)}{\be},
 \qquad
 \int_{\T^\d}u_{\be,x_0}\,\dd\muunif=0,
 \qquad
 \rho_{\be,x_0}=\frac{e^{u_{\be,x_0}}}{\int_{\T^\d}e^{u_{\be,x_0}}\,\dd\muunif},
 \label{eq:intro-delta-rho}
\end{equation}
one has, for every fixed Sobolev index \(s\geq0\), uniformly in \(x_0\),
\begin{equation}
 u_{\be,x_0}(x)
 =2\sqrt{\frac{\delta}{\kappa_\d}}
 \sum_{j=1}^\d\cos\bigl(2\pi(x_j-x_{0,j})\bigr)
 +O_{H^s}(\delta),
 \qquad x_0\in\T^\d.
 \label{eq:intro-onset-branch}
\end{equation}
The pressure satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \Pc_\d(\be)
 =\frac{\d}{2\kappa_\d}
 \left(1-\frac{\betas(\d)}{\be}\right)^2
 +O_\d\bigl((\be-\betas(\d))^3\bigr)
 \quad\text{as }\be\downarrow\betas(\d).
 \label{eq:intro-pressure-onset}
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \Cc_\d(A)
 =\frac{\d}{2\kappa_\d}
 \left(1-\frac{A}{\As(\d)}\right)^2
 +O_\d\left(\left(1-\frac{A}{\As(\d)}\right)^3\right)
 \quad\text{as }A\uparrow\As(\d).
 \label{eq:intro-C-onset}
\end{equation}

