rows.old_statement_tex:
\label{lem:selection-full-entropy-domain}\label{cor:common-selection}

Let $\d\ge2$ and $0<\lambda<\lambda_\d$, and set

\begin{equation}
 F_\lambda(\rho)=\Ent(\rho)-\frac\lambda2\Qcal_\d(\rho).
\end{equation}

\begin{enumerate}[(i)]

\item The functional $F_\lambda$ attains its minimum among all probability densities of finite entropy. Every minimizer $\rho$ is a smooth strictly positive Gibbs density.

\item For any minimizer $\rho$, let $\rho^\star$ be obtained by successive Steiner rearrangements in each coordinate. Then $\rho^\star$ is a minimizer and

\begin{equation}
 F_\lambda(\rho^\star)=F_\lambda(\rho),\qquad
 \Ent(\rho^\star)=\Ent(\rho).
\end{equation}

With $u^\star=\lambda K_\d*\rho^\star$, the pair $(u^\star,\rho^\star)$ is a smooth Euler pair satisfying \eqref{eq:euler}. Both functions are separately even and nonincreasing in each angular coordinate on $[0,\pi]$, and $u^\star$ has mean zero.

\item The density $\rho^\star$ has the mixture representation \eqref{eq:mixture}. Both $\rho^\star$ and $u^\star$ have nonnegative Fourier coefficients. Moreover, $\rho\not\equiv1$ implies $\rho^\star\not\equiv1$.

\end{enumerate}

